      "id": "start",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Let's learn consecutive and patterned averages with a small example.\n\nWe will build the method one step at a time and check each answer.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "concept_1"
        }
      ]
    },
    "concept_1": {
      "id": "concept_1",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "For the first n natural numbers, the chapter uses:\n\n1+2+...+n = n(n+1)/2.\n\nSo their average is:\n[n(n+1)/2] ÷ n = (n+1)/2.\n\nFor the first 40 natural numbers, this gives 20.5, exactly as in the chapter example.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_1"
        }
      ]
    },
