    "recap": {
      "id": "recap",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Patterned lists can save work.\n\nFirst n natural numbers: average = (n+1)/2.\nFirst n multiples of k: average = k(n+1)/2.\nFor equally spaced lists, the mean is the midpoint of the first and last terms.\nBut always identify the correct observations before using a shortcut.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
